WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:05.020
Sukuna is Hisoka on steroids.

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.590
Just like probably the most iconic character
in Hunter x Hunter, the king of curses is

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:15.460
loved for his charisma, is purely driven by
his sadistic hedonism and serves as a complete

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:20.620
wild card in the story, helping both the heroes
and the villains, just as often as he likes

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:27.789
to hurt or straight out ignore them, always
looking for a way to benefit himself.

00:00:27.789 --> 00:00:38.489
And yet, despite his cruelty, selfishness
and darkness, just like the psychopathic clown,

00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:44.180
the king of curses is as popular with fans
as most of the "good guys".

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:48.309
What exactly is it that makes Sukuna so fascinating
to watch?

00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:53.530
As I've already mentioned in previous videos,
Akutami loves taking popular tropes from anime

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:56.420
and manga, merge them and improve on them.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:01:02.109
and so, it comes as no big surprise that Sukuna
emerges as one of the most rounded, complex

00:01:02.109 --> 00:01:05.110
and intriguing villains, I have ever come
across.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:10.250
So let's discuss his background, his role
in the Story, his relationship to Itadori,

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:15.250
Megumi and Gojo and whether or not he truly
is all evil.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:30.180
This is the story of Ryoumen Sukuna.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:34.970
Sukuna is introduced in the story as the king
of curses, who lived over a thousand years

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:39.990
ago in the golden age of jujutsu in ancient
Japan, where he was the most powerful being

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:48.560
alive, despite being an actual human.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:54.040
As Akutami clarified in an interview however,
he wasn't so much a cursed user as a "natural

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:55.040
calamity."

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:59.020
Apparently he still remembers his past life
as a human as well.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:04.320
After his death however, he became a cursed
spirit, so powerful, that his body could not

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:08.220
be destroyed, but had to be divided into parts
and sealed away.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:09.220
- My god.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:13.629
This man akutami really has a rich imagination
to come up with something like - hm?

00:02:13.629 --> 00:02:19.549
- aaaand I'm being told that that this is
actually based on Japanese History.

00:02:19.549 --> 00:02:27.459
It's time for a short Japanese history lesson.

00:02:27.459 --> 00:02:37.219
Because, as it turns out, Ryoumen Sukuna,
is actually a historic figure.

00:02:37.219 --> 00:02:38.900
Well, kind of.

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:44.430
This person is mentioned in the second oldest
record of Japans history, the Nihon Shoki,

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.220
completed in the 8th century ad.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:50.989
Admittedly though, parts of it cross heavily
into mythology and shinto religion, so it

00:02:50.989 --> 00:02:54.799
is often impossible to separate legend from
fact.

00:02:54.799 --> 00:02:59.689
In this book however, that is filled with
myths and politics alike, Sukuna is described

00:02:59.689 --> 00:03:06.190
as a demon-like person, significantly taller
than any human with two faces, two arms and

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:07.230
two legs.

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:11.139
The epithet Ryoumen by the way, literally
meaning two-faced.

00:03:11.139 --> 00:03:16.830
He is said to have appeared in Hida prefecture,
todays Gifu, that you can see on the map here,

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:21.909
see, here's Tokyo, that didn't exist back
then, that's Gifu.

00:03:21.909 --> 00:03:25.680
I don't want you finishing this video without
having learned anything.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:26.680
Anyways.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:32.569
Here he terrorized the people, until a brave
military commander was able to expel him from

00:03:32.569 --> 00:03:33.569
the land.

00:03:33.569 --> 00:03:37.450
Interestingly enough however, while the Nihon
Shoki described him as a villain and an enemy

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:43.530
of the emperor, people in Hida and Mino Provinces
treated Ryomen-sukuna as a hero and benefactor

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.150
and worshipped him.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:50.719
And there is actually a shrine dedicated to
Sukuna still existing in Gifu prefecture,

00:03:50.719 --> 00:03:56.950
which a statue - that - doesn't look quite
as cool as this.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:06.120
[switch between epic sukuna anime and that
statue with epic loud music and derpy quiet

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.120
music] Bless Anime.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:10.390
Now, since there is still very little that
we know about him, I think the best way to

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:15.310
understand Sukuna's character is by looking
at his three most defining relationships so

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:19.030
far, that each give us a different perspective
on his personality.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:24.630
These relationships are Gojo, Itadori and
Megumi, who has long been teased to play a

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:32.940
central role 
in the story.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:37.070
As you might remember from my analysis of
gojo's character, there are a lot parallels

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:38.320
between these two.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:42.420
Being the two most self-centered and individualistic
characters in the story, both were introduced

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:46.940
pretty much at the same time, right at the
beginning of the story, one as the strongest

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:50.250
sorcerer and one as the king of curses.

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:56.230
And the two of them clearly share this incredible
aura of power, superiority and total control,

00:04:56.230 --> 00:05:04.380
especially during battle.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:09.970
next to their immense charisma, both of them
also value strength over all else.

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:15.220
In a way though, both are also incredibly
immature and cruel, playing with other people,

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:24.600
and especially Sukuna turning every fight
into 

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:28.250
a game.

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:33.260
These parallels that akutami draws between
the two, strongly suggest, that these two

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:35.690
will face off again at some point in the story.

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:40.220
And yet, there are also some striking differences
between the two, that I think will help us

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:42.970
explain sukuna's character a little better.

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:48.900
The most fundamental difference here, is of
course that gojo is a good guy and sukuna

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:49.950
a baddy.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:55.740
But since we are dealing with a lot of morally
grey and quite complex characters here, let's

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:57.390
not be that superficial.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:01.530
The main moral difference between the two
lies in their approach towards the central

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:04.000
moral question of jujutsu Kaisen.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.110
What constitutes a good life worth living?

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:10.760
For gojo, the answer here is strength itself.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:15.060
When you are strong you can use that strength
to shape the world as you please, which in

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:18.860
gojo's case means helping those he cares for.

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:21.190
Sukuna's approach is quite similar.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:26.930
However for him, a life worth living is the
most extreme form of hedonism, as he uses

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:33.480
his power to satisfy any of his desires, which
often include the mental or physical tormentation

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:40.060
of others.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:50.520
Gojo’s self confidence, always using his
strength for the sake of others and trying

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:55.520
to make a better world as he sees fit are
all good things, but the fact that he believes

00:06:55.520 --> 00:07:00.420
no matter how strong he becomes no matter
how hard he fights he’ll always die alone

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:05.390
because it’s not worth becoming close to
others in the Jujutsu World is the tragedy

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:06.390
of his character.

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:12.370
Whereas Sukuna in contrast either doesn’t
care or has reached a point of no return,

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:19.390
having become numb to the world around him
na living purely for and relying only on himself.

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:24.460
Same as with Hisoka however, as modern neuro
science has found, hedonism and living out

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:30.140
each and every one of your desires is anything
but equal to being happy or being fulfilled.

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:35.330
Instead, this sort of hedonistic lifestyle,
speaks for some sort of deep trauma in the

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:36.330
past.

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:41.480
Daniel Kahneman, an Israeli psychologist,
introduced the concepts of the experinencing,

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:43.460
vs the remembering self.

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:48.900
The Experiencing Self is the one that is experiencing
the emotional state in the moment, like eating

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:55.250
chocolate ice cream or you know tormenting
the teenager you are stuck in, while the remembering

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:59.730
self is the memory of the experienced moment
looking back.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:05.300
Thus, while relaxing at the beach in some
resort is probably a lot more fun while you're

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:11.740
there, exploring the history of Rome in the
heat of summer may suck while you're there,

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:15.210
but makes for way richer memory when thinking
back to it.

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:20.400
And bringing this all the way back to sukuna,
when someone is only living purely driven

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:25.670
by the experiencing self, this usually means
you prefer not to engage to much with your

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:28.450
past and long-term consequences.

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:33.490
What this tells us about the sadistic king
of courses, who used to be human after all,

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:38.769
is that he probably had a quite tragic past,
that drove him into abandoning his humanity.

00:08:38.769 --> 00:08:45.471
So, unlike Mahito, who Akutami described as
being evil by nature, I expect Sukuna to have

00:08:45.471 --> 00:08:51.509
a much more complex background as to why he
became as cruel and lust-driven as he has.

00:08:51.509 --> 00:09:03.999
That will be one hell off a backstory for
sure.

00:09:03.999 --> 00:09:08.990
Coming back to our comparison, while Gojo
was pretty much born with ridiculous strength

00:09:08.990 --> 00:09:14.149
and perception, and thus was used to having
the upper hand in battle, Sukuna, despite

00:09:14.149 --> 00:09:18.110
his power, is surprisingly focused during
all his battles.

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:23.240
No matter if against gojo or Megumi, he is
always analyzing his opponent, trying to figure

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:28.990
out exactly whats going on, so he can counter
as efficiently as possible.

00:09:28.990 --> 00:09:34.990
As he mentions, he appears to have an extremely
detailed understanding of what curses, cursed

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:42.050
energy and true jujutsu really are.

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:46.620
All of this would make a lot of sense, if
sukuna had to struggle his way to the top

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:49.790
from basically rock-bottom.

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:54.759
One last important parallel between Gojo and
Sukuna, in contrast to their individualism

00:09:54.759 --> 00:09:56.990
is their approach to others.

00:09:56.990 --> 00:10:01.589
While they both prefer to rely on their own
power, they both long to understand those

00:10:01.589 --> 00:10:05.139
around them, even if for different reasons.

00:10:05.139 --> 00:10:11.490
Sukuna’s one redeeming feature for now,
is that when people are strong he will acknowledge

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:16.129
them and actually finds them interesting,
as we can see with Megumi.

00:10:16.129 --> 00:10:23.310
But bottom line is, Sukuna is so focused on
strength, to try and fill the emptiness inside

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:33.370
him, by satisfying his every desire.

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:38.670
Funnily enough, he shares that trait not only
with Gojo, but also with the main character,

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:40.360
Itadori Yuji.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:45.720
He is the third person, who also thinks that
power will help him live a good life by trying

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:48.100
to save as many people as possible.

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:54.339
And in regards to their relationship, Sukuna
not only bares similarities to Hisoka, but

00:10:54.339 --> 00:11:00.529
also unites elements from stories like Naruto,
Bleach or Attack on Titan: The trope of the

00:11:00.529 --> 00:11:08.939
vessel.

00:11:08.939 --> 00:11:14.850
Just like Naruto and Eren, Itadori Yuji also
serves as the container for a source of immeasurable,

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:18.790
destructive power, that allow them to play
way above their league.

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:23.769
However, while the titan powers lack any personality
in themselves, and Kuruma turns out to be

00:11:23.769 --> 00:11:28.579
a lonely, misunderstood and used creature,
that doesn't want to get involved with Naruto

00:11:28.579 --> 00:11:35.040
or his life, Sukuna is an actual evil person,
that constantly talks to Itadori and actively

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:36.040
tries to harm him.

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:42.579
In that sense, I think that the closest comparison
that we can draw is with bleach, and by that

00:11:42.579 --> 00:11:50.910
I mean the good part of Bleach, and that is
with Hichigo, Ichigo's dark self.

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:55.509
An aspect of the self that is presented as
an antagonist.

00:11:55.509 --> 00:12:00.290
Have you ever wondered, why Sukuna looks so
much like Yuji?

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:06.230
We never see the face he originally had, he
always specifically takes Itadori’s form.

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:11.180
As we know, while the part of sukuna inside
Itadori would die, if he were to die, the

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:14.869
parts of his soul in the remaining fingers
would survive.

00:12:14.869 --> 00:12:20.160
So this Sukuna we have met, in a unique way
seems to be tied to Itadori.

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:25.220
Whenever Itadori can't control his darkest
emotions like fear or anger, he starts to

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:31.889
loose control over Sukuna, in other words
giving in to his own hedonistic instincts.

00:12:31.889 --> 00:12:40.790
For example, once Itadori consciously acknowledges
his anger towards Todo, he’s able to deal

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:42.439
with it in a more healthy way.

00:12:42.439 --> 00:12:48.029
And so, just like Ichigo had to take control
over his shadow self to use his powers, similarly

00:12:48.029 --> 00:12:54.589
it will be necessary for Itadori to take control
over sukuna, who only acknowledges strength,

00:12:54.589 --> 00:13:00.369
In order to actually profit form his powers
and keep him from hurting others and especially

00:13:00.369 --> 00:13:01.369
himself.

00:13:01.369 --> 00:13:08.320
Because the only person Sukuna is actually
fixated on, is not Itadori, whom he simply

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:11.560
finds irritating, but Megumi Fushiguro.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:20.620
What a transition.

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:25.879
Fushiguro in himself is such a fantastic character,
that he deserves a video of his own, which

00:13:25.879 --> 00:13:28.119
will be the next one after this.

00:13:28.119 --> 00:13:33.149
Luckily, Sukuna is not exactly interested
in Fushiguro for his personality, but for

00:13:33.149 --> 00:13:34.149
his abilities.

00:13:34.149 --> 00:13:39.149
The connection between the two has been hinted
at since their encounter during the cursed

00:13:39.149 --> 00:13:40.149
womb arc.

00:13:40.149 --> 00:13:45.069
And just to get it out of the way: of course
Sukuna wants to use Fushiguro for his own

00:13:45.069 --> 00:13:46.410
purposes.

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:58.879
Either to regain his own body or to take on
gojo, once he has.

00:13:58.879 --> 00:14:04.639
These statements were triggers for both Megumi
and the audience alike, but for different

00:14:04.639 --> 00:14:05.749
reasons.

00:14:05.749 --> 00:14:10.240
Sukuna’s words show that he has an interest
in Megumi and his ability while giving the

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:16.660
audience a more in-depth idea of Sukuna’s
tauntful personality . At the same time they

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:27.949
actually help Fushiguro to grow, something
Sukuna keeps encouraging.

00:14:27.949 --> 00:14:33.679
In this moment Megumi prepares to use what
Gojo calls his “Trump Card” an attack

00:14:33.679 --> 00:14:38.679
that is unconfirmed in nature, but seemingly
is the end all be all for Megumi.

00:14:38.679 --> 00:14:44.620
And funnily enough, both him and Gojo have
much more faith in his abilities than he himself

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:45.959
seems to.

00:14:45.959 --> 00:14:51.709
Whatever he sees in Megumi, it seems to make
it worth reviving Itadori and staying in his

00:14:51.709 --> 00:14:55.670
body, something he's not exactly enjoying.

00:14:55.670 --> 00:15:00.730
Yuji being a one in a million potential vessel
was a breaking point for Sukuna to once again

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:05.790
feel human flesh but we know he doesn’t
want to stay in Yuji’s body permanently,

00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:06.790
why not?

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:10.720
After all, Yuji can control his possession
and can become stronger as he absorbs more

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:11.720
fingers.

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:16.430
And should he die, the fingers within him
would actually die, unlike with curses where

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:21.629
the fingers would just appear where the curse
once was as they cannot be destroyed by normal

00:15:21.629 --> 00:15:29.399
means.

00:15:29.399 --> 00:15:34.440
And so it will be truly fascinating to see
how Sukuna's plan with Fushiguro will play

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:39.860
out, whether Itadori will be able to get his
respect and if we will ever get a true battle

